1
00:02:26,771 --> 00:02:29,024
Une biére, s'il vous plaît.

2
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:50,337
Merci.

3
00:04:34,816 --> 00:04:36,276
We are closed.

4
00:04:36,401 --> 00:04:38,111
Just a small drink.

5
00:04:44,868 --> 00:04:46,870
The toilets ?

6
00:05:39,839 --> 00:05:43,551
A quick drink and then l'll leave.

7
00:05:46,596 --> 00:05:48,473
Why are you rushing off ?

8
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:51,768
- Hmm ?
- l said, why are you rushing off ?

9
00:05:51,893 --> 00:05:53,561
l don't understand.

10
00:05:54,938 --> 00:05:56,815
The man from Bristol called ya.

11
00:06:02,654 --> 00:06:05,198
- What man ?
- The man in the wheelchair.

12
00:06:41,901 --> 00:06:44,279
What were you doing back here ?

13
00:06:45,905 --> 00:06:47,282
Lady,

14
00:06:47,407 --> 00:06:50,952
l never walk into a place
l don't know how to walk out of.

15
00:06:52,203 --> 00:06:54,080
Then why would you get into that van ?

16
00:06:54,205 --> 00:06:56,583
You know the reason.

17
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:09,823
Make yourselves at home.

18
00:08:09,948 --> 00:08:12,450
You've come a long way.

19
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:15,537
- Thanks for coming.
- What's the job ?

20
00:08:15,704 --> 00:08:19,416
There's some people
who have something we require.

21
00:08:19,582 --> 00:08:22,961
- And we want you to get it from them.
- lt involves shooting ?

22
00:08:24,129 --> 00:08:26,673
You must be tired.

23
00:08:26,798 --> 00:08:28,967
We'll tell you more tomorrow.

24
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:39,769
Seven fat years
and seven lean years.

25
00:08:39,894 --> 00:08:42,689
- That's what it says in the Bible.
- You ever kill anybody ?

26
00:08:42,814 --> 00:08:45,358
l hurt somebody's feelings once.

27
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:53,658
Don't l know you ?

28
00:08:55,702 --> 00:08:59,205
l don't think so. l'd remember.

29
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:08,214
Okay, two-hour shifts.

30
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:11,051
l'll watch the front,
you guys watch the back.

31
00:09:13,345 --> 00:09:14,888
Merci.

32
00:09:27,776 --> 00:09:29,611
You awake, then ?

33
00:09:31,488 --> 00:09:34,032
Hmm ?

34
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:38,411
How we doin' ?

35
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:44,626
Yep.

36
00:10:02,894 --> 00:10:04,771
You labour or management ?

37
00:10:05,021 --> 00:10:09,025
lf l was management,
l wouldn't have given you a cigarette.

38
00:10:10,777 --> 00:10:14,781
l am the tour guide.
Over there is the Eiffel Tower.

39
00:10:14,906 --> 00:10:17,617
Over here, the Louvre.
Over there, les toilettes.

40
00:10:17,784 --> 00:10:20,078
What do l call you ?

41
00:10:20,245 --> 00:10:22,914
- My name is Vincent.
- Sam.

42
00:10:26,167 --> 00:10:30,839
As per the agreement,
your salary will be $5,000 a week

43
00:10:30,964 --> 00:10:33,633
with a minimum
of four weeks' work.

44
00:10:33,758 --> 00:10:36,136
On the successful completion
of the mission,

45
00:10:36,302 --> 00:10:40,098
you will each receive
a bonus of $20,000.

46
00:10:41,599 --> 00:10:45,645
And by the way,
my name is Deirdre.

47
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:48,690
- The broad outlines of the mission are...
- Who are your principals ?

48
00:10:48,857 --> 00:10:50,650
For you,
there's no one but myself.

49
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:52,777
Huh ?

50
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:55,864
And what can we infer
from your charming lrish lilt ?

51
00:10:56,031 --> 00:10:59,075
- Anything you like.
- Where's the equipment ?

52
00:10:59,242 --> 00:11:01,745
Tell me what you need, make a list,
and give it to Vincent.

53
00:11:01,870 --> 00:11:05,081
- Some of the equipment's quite technical.
- lf it's in Paris, l'll find it.

54
00:11:05,206 --> 00:11:08,668
This is what we're after.

55
00:11:08,835 --> 00:11:12,756
We need to take it intact from several
men who'll be intent on preventing us.

56
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:15,133
- How many men ?
- You American ?

57
00:11:15,258 --> 00:11:19,095
l think the group will be between
five and eight. No more than eight.

58
00:11:19,262 --> 00:11:23,767
- You don't know for sure ?
- Not now but l will know before the event.

59
00:11:23,892 --> 00:11:27,395
lf you don't know,
why say between five and eight ?

60
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,397
There's two to three cars.
The group's travellin'.

61
00:11:29,522 --> 00:11:30,857
- They're not in Paris ?
- No.

62
00:11:30,982 --> 00:11:31,858
Where are they ?

63
00:11:32,025 --> 00:11:34,569
- You'll find out soon enough.
- What's in the case ?

64
00:11:36,321 --> 00:11:39,240
Our plan, in broad strokes, is an ambush.

65
00:11:39,407 --> 00:11:41,910
lt's to hit the car,
to take them in transit.

66
00:11:42,077 --> 00:11:45,789
- Transit ? City ? Country ?
- Right now, as l said, l don't know.

67
00:11:45,914 --> 00:11:48,291
But we've to move very quickly.

68
00:11:48,416 --> 00:11:52,837
We'll start with this: Ambush
and assault on two to three vehicles,

69
00:11:52,962 --> 00:11:57,634
five to eight men, and our objective
is the safe retrieval of this case.

70
00:11:57,759 --> 00:12:01,429
Tell Vincent
what it is you'll need.

71
00:12:01,554 --> 00:12:06,393
What do we know about them ?
Are they French ? Who are they ?

72
00:12:06,518 --> 00:12:09,813
All you need to know right now
is that they're very unpleasant.

73
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:14,526
- You've done this kind of thing before ?
- You know...

74
00:12:14,651 --> 00:12:15,735
How difficult can it be ?

75
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:17,946
We have no idea
how these men will be armed ?

76
00:12:18,113 --> 00:12:20,490
lt seems they'll be
very well armed, indeed.

77
00:12:20,657 --> 00:12:22,659
Where are we going and
how are we getting back from there ?

78
00:12:22,784 --> 00:12:25,912
lt'll be in France, and the group
will disband at the RV point.

79
00:12:26,037 --> 00:12:29,666
- What does she mean ?
- After that, we're on our own.

80
00:12:29,791 --> 00:12:32,460
- lt's a military term.
- That's right.

81
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:34,129
Larry, tell Vincent what you'll need.

82
00:12:34,254 --> 00:12:39,134
Something very fast. Audi S-8.
Something that can shove.

83
00:12:39,259 --> 00:12:41,970
l'm going to have it for you
by the afternoon.

84
00:12:42,137 --> 00:12:45,765
l'll also need a nitrous system.
l've got the specs.

85
00:12:50,478 --> 00:12:52,856
What do you use, weapons-wise ?

86
00:12:53,023 --> 00:12:55,191
- Hmm ?
- Weapons.

87
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:58,361
- l'm a... l'm a weapons man.
- Weapons man.

88
00:12:58,486 --> 00:13:00,363
- Yeah.
- Okay.

89
00:13:00,530 --> 00:13:04,492
They tend to settle the argument.
So what do you favour ?

90
00:13:04,659 --> 00:13:08,204
Well, you know. lt's a toolbox.
You put the tools in for the job.

91
00:13:08,371 --> 00:13:09,497
What ?

92
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:12,709
You know,
l actually favour the old 191 1 .

93
00:13:12,834 --> 00:13:16,212
.45. Old gun.

94
00:13:18,089 --> 00:13:20,175
lt served my country well.
A long time.

95
00:13:20,342 --> 00:13:22,677
Your country !

96
00:13:22,844 --> 00:13:24,846
Not done too well, have you,
last few wars ?

97
00:13:25,013 --> 00:13:27,390
Perhaps not, but at least
we don't go around whining about it.

98
00:13:30,060 --> 00:13:30,810
You ex-military ?

99
00:13:30,935 --> 00:13:32,896
No, l got my job
through the New York Times.

100
00:13:34,522 --> 00:13:37,776
- Don't let him get you down.
- lt don't mean nothin' to me.

101
00:13:37,901 --> 00:13:39,694
l say what l think.

102
00:13:39,819 --> 00:13:42,238
Are you ex-military ?

103
00:13:42,405 --> 00:13:44,574
Boys at Hereford ?

104
00:13:44,741 --> 00:13:47,410
l'm sorry, but l'd like to go backwards.
The line of retreat is...

105
00:13:47,494 --> 00:13:51,998
She just told you.
We meet back at the RV, disband.

106
00:13:52,165 --> 00:13:56,086
l understand. l'm just trying to get
a vague notion of the opposition.

107
00:13:56,211 --> 00:14:01,883
We're gonna cause some animosity.
How many will be coming after us ?

108
00:14:02,050 --> 00:14:05,053
- You worried about your own skin ?
- Yeah, l am.

109
00:14:05,178 --> 00:14:07,055
lt covers my body.

110
00:14:08,515 --> 00:14:11,851
All your concerns will be addressed
before we leave.

111
00:14:12,018 --> 00:14:14,479
- Electronics and commo.
- Not more than three cars ?

112
00:14:14,604 --> 00:14:15,980
That is our information.

113
00:14:16,231 --> 00:14:18,817
- Can you get me a simulator ?
- What's a simulator ?

114
00:14:18,942 --> 00:14:22,153
Gunpowder. Sound only, no lead.
Sounds like a pistol.

115
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:23,822
Quite diverting.

116
00:14:23,947 --> 00:14:27,575
Listen, l'm also gonna need
some bigger injection jets.

117
00:14:27,701 --> 00:14:30,370
The Bosch is not gonna do it.
They have to be custom-made.

118
00:14:30,453 --> 00:14:33,415
We going north ? We going south ?

119
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:36,751
l'd like some new clothes.

120
00:14:36,876 --> 00:14:39,546
- Vincent will sort you out.
- l'll take care of it.

121
00:14:46,428 --> 00:14:49,556
- So what brought you here ?
- A fella that doesn't work so well.

122
00:14:50,932 --> 00:14:53,268
The man in the wheelchair ?

123
00:14:54,185 --> 00:14:55,645
How did he get there ?

124
00:14:55,770 --> 00:15:00,567
That was in your neck of the woods,
back in the late unpleasantness.

125
00:15:11,953 --> 00:15:13,246
Good reflexes.

126
00:15:14,789 --> 00:15:16,541
Oh, yeah.

127
00:15:17,083 --> 00:15:19,252
They die hard.

128
00:15:26,217 --> 00:15:29,804
- lnterrogation.
- What ?

129
00:15:29,929 --> 00:15:33,975
- Methods to withstand interrogation.
- You've done that ?

130
00:15:34,142 --> 00:15:37,062
We were taught
to hold out indefinitely.

131
00:15:38,897 --> 00:15:42,609
- Nobody can hold out indefinitely.
- Ah, is that so ?

132
00:15:42,734 --> 00:15:48,323
Everybody has a limit. l spent
some time in interrogation... once.

133
00:15:48,448 --> 00:15:50,784
- They make it hard on you ?
- They don't make it easy.

134
00:15:51,159 --> 00:15:55,205
Yeah, it was unpleasant.
l held out as long as l could.

135
00:15:55,330 --> 00:15:57,999
All the stuff they tried.

136
00:15:58,124 --> 00:16:00,418
You just can't hold out for ever.

137
00:16:00,543 --> 00:16:03,213
- lmpossible.
- How'd they finally get to you ?

138
00:16:03,380 --> 00:16:06,091
- They gave me a grasshopper.
- What's a grasshopper ?

139
00:16:06,257 --> 00:16:10,720
That's two part gin, two part brandy,
one part créme de menthe...

140
00:16:10,887 --> 00:16:12,889
Fuckin' smartass !

141
00:16:13,807 --> 00:16:16,768
- Can you find this place ?
- Of course.

142
00:16:16,935 --> 00:16:18,812
l know it.

143
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:21,940
That's where
they wanna do the exchange.

144
00:16:22,107 --> 00:16:23,900
You're gonna exchange for cash ?

145
00:16:24,943 --> 00:16:29,030
- You know these people ?
- My people know them.

146
00:16:29,197 --> 00:16:31,408
Your people have done business
with them before ?

147
00:16:31,533 --> 00:16:34,327
Or these people
just gave your people a number ?

148
00:16:45,130 --> 00:16:47,382
Larry.

149
00:16:51,094 --> 00:16:54,723
Okay. lf we're gonna do it,
let's do the goddamn thing right.

150
00:16:57,642 --> 00:17:00,395
- Hey !
- l'm busy.

151
00:17:01,688 --> 00:17:03,982
Okay, come on. Let's go.

152
00:17:04,149 --> 00:17:07,610
The answers to your questions
l'll know when l get back.

153
00:17:07,736 --> 00:17:10,822
- l'll go with you.
- Go with them.

154
00:17:31,134 --> 00:17:32,969
Who does this girl work for ?

155
00:17:33,094 --> 00:17:37,432
Well, she works for our betters.

156
00:17:37,557 --> 00:17:40,727
lt seems that's what
we're meant to know.

157
00:17:48,526 --> 00:17:51,488
Always a waiting game.

158
00:17:51,613 --> 00:17:55,408
- What ?
- lt's a waiting game.

159
00:17:57,952 --> 00:18:01,206
Hey, wait.
Would you not do that, please ?

160
00:18:03,333 --> 00:18:06,378
Bad for the night vision, yeah ?

161
00:18:12,592 --> 00:18:14,844
There they are.

162
00:19:03,184 --> 00:19:05,854
- You have the list ?
- Yes, l have it.

163
00:19:06,021 --> 00:19:07,689
Give it to me.

164
00:19:11,026 --> 00:19:13,528
Money ?

165
00:19:14,821 --> 00:19:17,323
Okay. You follow my lead.

166
00:19:17,490 --> 00:19:19,701
Just make sure you watch my back.

167
00:19:24,497 --> 00:19:26,166
Don't make any sudden moves.

168
00:19:26,666 --> 00:19:30,211
Just because we're buying guns
doesn't mean we didn't bring any.

169
00:19:30,337 --> 00:19:33,590
Don't worry. Everything's fine.

170
00:19:36,259 --> 00:19:38,845
You want to back him up ?

171
00:19:42,849 --> 00:19:44,934
What would l profit from your death ?

172
00:19:45,060 --> 00:19:48,480
- Well, you'd have the money.
- l have the money already.

173
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:52,859
l'll watch the back.

174
00:19:56,988 --> 00:19:58,573
- Have you got it all ?
- Oui.

175
00:20:00,450 --> 00:20:03,787
- You're sure ?
- Ofcourse. Come and see.

176
00:20:14,130 --> 00:20:15,090
There it is "

177
00:20:35,110 --> 00:20:37,529
lt's not all here.

178
00:20:39,489 --> 00:20:41,700
- Vincent.
- What ?

179
00:20:45,704 --> 00:20:48,373
lt's not all here.

180
00:20:48,498 --> 00:20:50,291
- C'est tout ?
- Ah, non, non, non.

181
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:54,713
Le patron va contrôler l'argent.
Vous aurez le reste de la marchandise.

182
00:20:54,838 --> 00:20:58,842
Tiens. ll est lá dans la voiture,
avec le patron.

183
00:20:58,967 --> 00:21:03,388
He said the rest is in the other car.
The boss wants to check the money.

184
00:21:03,513 --> 00:21:06,683
lfhe agrees, we have no problem.

185
00:21:06,808 --> 00:21:08,601
Here, take the car keys.

186
00:21:08,727 --> 00:21:11,771
Go on. Take them.

187
00:21:15,650 --> 00:21:17,444
Come on. Come.

188
00:21:19,070 --> 00:21:21,781
Okay, give me...
Give me some of the money.

189
00:21:28,997 --> 00:21:31,958
Give me some of the money !

190
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:36,212
- Okay.
- You aren't going in there ?

191
00:21:36,338 --> 00:21:40,467
- Yeah, l am, and so are you.
- Why am l going in there ?

192
00:21:40,633 --> 00:21:44,596
- Why ? To protect me.
- There is no protection there.

193
00:21:44,721 --> 00:21:48,183
lf it's a come-on, we're fish in a barrel.
Why do they want you in there ?

194
00:21:48,308 --> 00:21:50,685
- What are you, crazy ?
- You know, you think too hard.

195
00:21:50,852 --> 00:21:54,439
Nobody ever told me that before.
But l wouldn't go in there.

196
00:21:56,191 --> 00:21:59,652
- What is it, Sam ?
- l don't like it. Look at it.

197
00:22:01,363 --> 00:22:03,198
Okay, okay.

198
00:22:03,365 --> 00:22:05,742
Okay, let's just do it.
Let's just do it and be done, yeah ?

199
00:22:06,743 --> 00:22:08,119
You don't wanna go in there.

200
00:22:09,704 --> 00:22:13,625
- l'm getting paid to go. lt's that simple.
- Okay, come on. Let's go.

201
00:22:13,750 --> 00:22:17,337
lf anything goes down,
get next to one of those guys.

202
00:22:17,462 --> 00:22:19,589
lf there's a sniper,
he'll be afraid to shoot his own guy.

203
00:22:19,756 --> 00:22:21,383
- Let's go !
- All right.

204
00:22:43,571 --> 00:22:45,448
Stop !

205
00:22:45,573 --> 00:22:47,742
Stay where you are.

206
00:23:03,633 --> 00:23:06,219
So, everything's fine.

207
00:23:17,188 --> 00:23:19,190
Shit ! l can't see ! l can't see !

208
00:23:32,245 --> 00:23:34,122
Have some of this !

209
00:23:38,793 --> 00:23:40,337
Fuckin' arsehole !

210
00:23:44,966 --> 00:23:48,094
Fuckin' have some more, you bastards !

211
00:23:49,846 --> 00:23:51,723
Come on ! Come on !

212
00:23:53,183 --> 00:23:55,560
Let's go !

213
00:23:55,727 --> 00:23:59,939
- No ! You goddamn...
- Come on ! Let's go !

214
00:24:12,994 --> 00:24:14,913
- ls anybody hurt ?
- We're fine.

215
00:24:16,915 --> 00:24:21,670
Almost a bit of raspberry jam
back there, yeah ?

216
00:24:21,795 --> 00:24:23,672
A bit of raspberry jam back there !

217
00:24:27,425 --> 00:24:31,096
Got the swag, kept the money.
Job well done.

218
00:24:31,221 --> 00:24:33,098
That's a fact. That is a fact.

219
00:24:58,623 --> 00:24:59,708
Slow down. Slow down.

220
00:25:01,835 --> 00:25:03,962
l think l have to stop.

221
00:25:32,907 --> 00:25:33,742
Thank you.

222
00:25:45,378 --> 00:25:47,213
Why did you take this job ?

223
00:25:49,799 --> 00:25:51,801
My friend, l need the money.

224
00:25:52,969 --> 00:25:55,305
The money is here.

225
00:25:59,642 --> 00:26:02,771
That's what this is, you know ? Money.

226
00:26:06,900 --> 00:26:08,777
Yeah, but who are our employers ?

227
00:26:11,446 --> 00:26:13,281
You're right.

228
00:26:41,810 --> 00:26:43,645
Excuse me.

229
00:26:43,812 --> 00:26:46,314
Excuse me, monsieur.

230
00:26:55,156 --> 00:26:57,492
The Russians are bidding for the case.

231
00:26:57,617 --> 00:27:01,621
The case is in Nice.
They're trying to sell it to the Russians.

232
00:27:01,746 --> 00:27:05,000
They're staying at
the Villa Belle Mer in Nice.

233
00:27:06,167 --> 00:27:10,630
- The team isn't ready.
- Whatever the team is, you do it now.

234
00:27:10,755 --> 00:27:13,842
The Russians have decided to bid.
We need to move now.

235
00:27:14,009 --> 00:27:16,011
Excuse me.

236
00:27:16,261 --> 00:27:19,639
l have the information.
We'll be movin' very soon.

237
00:27:19,806 --> 00:27:21,683
lt'll definitely
be in the nature of an ambush

238
00:27:21,850 --> 00:27:25,645
somewhere between here and here.

239
00:27:25,812 --> 00:27:30,191
We'll anticipate
a three-car convoy with a backup team.

240
00:27:30,316 --> 00:27:33,820
We will try and stop the target
before they can get away from us.

241
00:27:33,987 --> 00:27:35,905
- What's in the case ?
- That information isn't necessary.

242
00:27:36,072 --> 00:27:38,033
ls it heavy ? ls it explosive ?

243
00:27:38,199 --> 00:27:40,160
ls it chained
