they use them for different things.

486
00:59:56,638 --> 00:59:57,514
l need your help.

487
00:59:59,224 --> 01:00:01,059
- l thought you left.
- l did leave.

488
01:00:01,226 --> 01:00:03,395
- You did leave ? You're out ?
- That's right.

489
01:00:03,520 --> 01:00:05,855
Can you help me ? l need your help.

490
01:00:07,899 --> 01:00:09,734
What's the number ?

491
01:00:14,155 --> 01:00:16,991
Yeah, the post office is, uh,
just down to your left.

492
01:00:17,158 --> 01:00:18,868
- Up on the left ? Thanks.
- On the left.

493
01:00:26,876 --> 01:00:30,672
- A friend of yours ?
- We went to high school together.

494
01:00:30,839 --> 01:00:34,092
Everyone's your brother
until the rent comes due.

495
01:00:34,217 --> 01:00:35,760
Ain't that the truth !

496
01:00:35,927 --> 01:00:38,346
Yes. Yes, on the terrace ?

497
01:00:38,805 --> 01:00:40,223
Facing me ? l see him.

498
01:00:40,348 --> 01:00:43,393
Yes, l'll get him. Hang on, please.

499
01:00:47,897 --> 01:00:49,357
Excuse me, sir. Are you Sam ?

500
01:00:52,360 --> 01:00:53,194
Yeah.

501
01:00:53,319 --> 01:00:54,738
Telephone for you.

502
01:01:03,663 --> 01:01:05,540
Yeah, good to see you, too.

503
01:01:05,665 --> 01:01:08,501
lf his position changes, l'll let you know.

504
01:01:15,216 --> 01:01:17,218
Gregor's in a town called Arles.

505
01:02:33,336 --> 01:02:35,714
He's at the arena.

506
01:03:08,163 --> 01:03:11,124
So this is the amphitheatre of Arles

507
01:03:11,291 --> 01:03:15,253
which was built
at the end of the first century AD.

508
01:03:15,420 --> 01:03:17,797
lt is built with limestone.

509
01:03:25,305 --> 01:03:26,556
l know those men.

510
01:03:58,880 --> 01:04:01,883
And you can see
this dominant yellow colour

511
01:04:02,008 --> 01:04:04,511
which is actually caused
essentially by a lantern.

512
01:04:04,636 --> 01:04:07,347
We're not sure that the walls
were actually yellow.

513
01:04:07,472 --> 01:04:09,349
And so, now we will continue

514
01:04:09,516 --> 01:04:12,102
and visit the Roman baths
down this way.

515
01:04:25,782 --> 01:04:27,617
Yeah.

516
01:04:30,161 --> 01:04:34,040
Thank you, gentlemen.
That'll do nicely.

517
01:04:36,001 --> 01:04:37,836
lt's Sergi. l remember you.

518
01:04:38,003 --> 01:04:40,714
Yes, Gregor, it's me.

519
01:04:40,839 --> 01:04:44,592
- How have you been ?
- Well. These are trying times.

520
01:04:44,759 --> 01:04:47,804
- l'm sorry about the unfortunate incident.
- Oh, yeah.

521
01:04:48,013 --> 01:04:51,391
lt was excessive.
And more to the point, it was foolish.

522
01:04:51,516 --> 01:04:54,227
l couldn't agree with you more.

523
01:04:54,352 --> 01:04:56,646
Mikhi did it without consulting me.

524
01:04:58,273 --> 01:05:00,984
Yeah, he's turned rogue
and can't be controlled, is that it ?

525
01:05:13,997 --> 01:05:16,708
Excusez-moi.
Je cherche la vieille maison de Van Gogh.

526
01:05:16,875 --> 01:05:19,919
- l don't... l don't...
- Oh, English.

527
01:05:20,045 --> 01:05:21,921
Sorry. Such a fool.

528
01:05:22,088 --> 01:05:23,923
l was looking for Van Gogh's old house.

529
01:05:24,049 --> 01:05:28,428
So what could have been conducted
in a collegial atmosphere

530
01:05:28,595 --> 01:05:30,638
is now fucked into a cocked hat.

531
01:05:30,764 --> 01:05:34,684
- What do you think ?
- l think we'll meet your price.

532
01:05:36,394 --> 01:05:40,482
Yeah. Yes, so let's see it. Let's see it now.

533
01:05:40,607 --> 01:05:41,983
Where do you have it, in your belt ?

534
01:05:42,192 --> 01:05:44,778
- Let's see it !
- Show me the case first.

535
01:05:47,113 --> 01:05:50,241
You're great in the locker room,
and your reflexes might die hard,

536
01:05:50,408 --> 01:05:52,243
but you're weak
when you put your spikes on.

537
01:05:53,870 --> 01:05:57,832
- Gregor ? Are you all right ?
- Gregor's fine.

538
01:05:57,999 --> 01:06:00,669
But l think you're in a wee spot of trouble.

539
01:06:01,795 --> 01:06:04,547
- Where is it ? Where is it ?
- l don't have it with me.

540
01:06:04,673 --> 01:06:05,632
Where ?

541
01:06:05,757 --> 01:06:08,218
l mailed it to myself.
A post-office box in Paris.

542
01:06:08,343 --> 01:06:09,344
Hilfe !

543
01:06:09,469 --> 01:06:11,137
Help ! He's robbing me !

544
01:06:50,343 --> 01:06:52,345
Pardon. Pardon.

545
01:06:52,512 --> 01:06:54,264
Pardon. Avancez !

546
01:06:54,431 --> 01:06:55,223
Pardon.

547
01:07:59,746 --> 01:08:00,538
Stop.

548
01:08:04,334 --> 01:08:07,003
- Where do l know you from ?
- Vienna.

549
01:08:07,128 --> 01:08:10,715
Of course. l'm sorry to have to do this.

550
01:08:10,840 --> 01:08:11,841
Hey !

551
01:08:30,193 --> 01:08:31,903
- Christ.
- Drive.

552
01:08:54,092 --> 01:08:59,180
Stop ! Descends ! Vite ! Descends !

553
01:09:16,406 --> 01:09:23,621
- l'm gonna have to take care of this.
- What do you want to do ?

554
01:09:23,747 --> 01:09:27,500
Uh, get to a doctor
or a veterinarian's office.

555
01:09:27,667 --> 01:09:29,878
l'll just boost what l need.

556
01:09:33,673 --> 01:09:37,302
- Could you do that ?
- Of course. l can do better.

557
01:09:40,055 --> 01:09:42,265
- How is it ?
- l'm leakin'.

558
01:09:43,683 --> 01:09:45,352
l'm sorry.

559
01:09:50,065 --> 01:09:51,900
That girl sold us out.

560
01:09:56,571 --> 01:09:59,407
She sold us out.

561
01:10:51,042 --> 01:10:53,962
- Ready, Jean-Pierre ?
- Everything's ready.

562
01:11:13,314 --> 01:11:15,275
Get my legs up.

563
01:11:15,400 --> 01:11:17,277
Careful.

564
01:11:26,870 --> 01:11:29,039
Are you sure you can do this ?

565
01:11:29,205 --> 01:11:32,751
Yeah. l once removed a guy's appendix
with a grapefruit spoon.

566
01:11:32,917 --> 01:11:36,129
- Have a drink.
- No booze. No.

567
01:11:41,885 --> 01:11:46,848
Easy, easy, easy.

568
01:11:52,896 --> 01:11:56,691
lt's just below the surface.

569
01:11:58,234 --> 01:12:01,363
All right, let's do it.
Just douse it with alcohol.

570
01:12:04,866 --> 01:12:07,327
Take the gauze and wipe away
as much of the blood as you can.

571
01:12:07,494 --> 01:12:09,621
Keep it clean so l can see it.

572
01:12:14,084 --> 01:12:15,960
Yeah. That's it.

573
01:12:22,842 --> 01:12:24,928
All right.
What we're gonna do is routine.

574
01:12:25,095 --> 01:12:27,597
l've done this many times before.

575
01:12:27,764 --> 01:12:29,891
There are no vital organs, arteries.
lt's okay.

576
01:12:30,058 --> 01:12:32,102
You won't kill me.
Just make sure you get the bullet

577
01:12:32,227 --> 01:12:34,270
- before you pry it out.
- All right.

578
01:12:34,437 --> 01:12:36,272
Take that scalpel.

579
01:12:40,819 --> 01:12:42,696
The upper part.

580
01:12:44,322 --> 01:12:46,282
Over here. Just cut up there.

581
01:12:46,408 --> 01:12:48,284
Just a little cut.

582
01:12:59,254 --> 01:13:01,089
Okay. Got it.

583
01:13:03,008 --> 01:13:04,843
Now take the clamp.

584
01:13:05,010 --> 01:13:07,679
Take the clamp and open up... the hole.

585
01:13:07,846 --> 01:13:10,390
Just put it in there.

586
01:13:11,516 --> 01:13:13,393
Put it in there.

587
01:13:13,518 --> 01:13:15,395
That's it. Put it in. Just...

588
01:13:15,562 --> 01:13:17,772
Now open it up. Spread it. Spread it.

589
01:13:17,897 --> 01:13:20,233
Okay. Okay.

590
01:13:20,358 --> 01:13:23,403
Now get the other...
Get the other clamps and get the bullet.

591
01:13:23,528 --> 01:13:25,530
Remember, don't take it out
unless you really got it.

592
01:13:44,007 --> 01:13:47,344
Do it again. Do it again.
Just try once more.

593
01:13:53,558 --> 01:13:57,145
l'm sorry.

594
01:13:59,105 --> 01:14:02,942
When he pulls it out, put the gauze in.
There's gonna be a lot of blood.

595
01:14:08,698 --> 01:14:10,533
Put the gauze there.

596
01:14:20,543 --> 01:14:22,879
Fucker sprayed his bullet with Teflon.

597
01:14:24,214 --> 01:14:28,051
He was trying to stamp me ''paid in full''.

598
01:14:28,259 --> 01:14:31,012
- ls that why it went through the vest ?
- Yeah.

599
01:14:32,806 --> 01:14:35,517
You think you can stitch me up
on your own ?

600
01:14:36,935 --> 01:14:40,522
lf you don't mind,
l'm gonna pass out.

601
01:15:30,238 --> 01:15:32,657
You gonna kill me ?

602
01:15:32,782 --> 01:15:36,661
No. l'm not gonna kill ya.

603
01:16:04,272 --> 01:16:06,107
Why would l want to kill ya ?

604
01:16:25,377 --> 01:16:28,296
- l gave you a job.
- l did my job.

605
01:16:29,506 --> 01:16:31,132
So how'd it go wrong ?

606
01:16:31,257 --> 01:16:33,259
l thought you wanted the case.

607
01:16:34,511 --> 01:16:36,262
Oh, we'll get the case.

608
01:16:36,388 --> 01:16:39,432
We'll get the case, eh, Gregor ?

609
01:16:41,184 --> 01:16:43,061
Don't you worry about the case.

610
01:16:45,563 --> 01:16:47,649
What l want's an explanation.

611
01:16:47,816 --> 01:16:50,485
An explanation ? For what ?

612
01:16:50,694 --> 01:16:52,612
You bollixed it up.

613
01:16:52,821 --> 01:16:55,740
- l bollixed it up ?
- You hired him.

614
01:16:55,865 --> 01:16:57,742
Through your fucking contact !

615
01:17:03,873 --> 01:17:07,502
- You didn't do your homework.
- Why did you have to kill Larry ?

616
01:17:07,627 --> 01:17:09,504
Oh, Larry, is it ?

617
01:17:10,672 --> 01:17:12,507
l was clearing up your mess.

618
01:17:12,632 --> 01:17:15,510
My mess ?
Oh, well, you take over, then.

619
01:17:15,677 --> 01:17:17,512
- Eh ?
- But you can't, can you ?

620
01:17:17,679 --> 01:17:19,806
lt's you that's hiding, isn't it, Seamus ?

621
01:17:19,973 --> 01:17:22,308
lt's you that can't show your face.

622
01:17:25,020 --> 01:17:28,440
Who else thinks that ?
Who you been talking to ?

623
01:17:28,606 --> 01:17:30,775
lsn't that the reason
why l'm doing this job ?

624
01:17:34,446 --> 01:17:36,281
You're a good girl, Deirdre.

625
01:17:37,699 --> 01:17:39,576
Do your job, eh ?

626
01:17:53,340 --> 01:17:55,425
He's tough, your Yank.

627
01:17:56,843 --> 01:17:58,428
You're right about that.

628
01:18:00,722 --> 01:18:01,931
But who is he ?

629
01:18:03,683 --> 01:18:05,477
That's not important.

630
01:18:06,519 --> 01:18:09,230
Didn't he work for the ClA ?

631
01:18:10,398 --> 01:18:12,150
He used to.

632
01:18:12,901 --> 01:18:14,361
Not anymore ?

633
01:18:15,987 --> 01:18:17,614
He's on the run.

634
01:18:19,157 --> 01:18:20,617
You're sure ?

635
01:18:20,742 --> 01:18:25,663
l know what he can do.
l've seen him.

636
01:18:25,789 --> 01:18:28,249
Why would he carve himselfup
ifhe were still ClA ?

637
01:18:28,375 --> 01:18:30,960
He makes a call and it's taken care of.

638
01:18:41,554 --> 01:18:43,515
And you ? How are you ?

639
01:18:52,315 --> 01:18:57,779
We need some information.
We need to find some people in Paris.

640
01:18:57,904 --> 01:18:58,863
Who ?

641
01:18:59,406 --> 01:19:02,075
An lrish man and woman,

642
01:19:02,200 --> 01:19:04,411
a German, an ex-KGB.

643
01:19:05,245 --> 01:19:06,329
They're professionals.

644
01:19:06,454 --> 01:19:07,914
They're in hiding.

645
01:19:08,623 --> 01:19:11,668
This is really important to you ?

646
01:19:13,920 --> 01:19:16,423
He saved my life.

647
01:19:19,342 --> 01:19:20,176
Bon.

648
01:19:22,637 --> 01:19:25,181
l'll find them for you.

649
01:19:43,950 --> 01:19:46,703
Where's the case ?

650
01:19:50,248 --> 01:19:52,083
lt will come tomorrow. l'm sure.

651
01:19:52,292 --> 01:19:55,795
Well, l'm sure it will, too. Let's go.

652
01:19:56,921 --> 01:19:59,215
Let's hope so, for your sake, anyway.

653
01:20:30,914 --> 01:20:33,041
Are you feeling better ?

654
01:20:33,208 --> 01:20:35,377
Yeah, enough to move around. Thanks.

655
01:20:45,345 --> 01:20:47,180
My hobby.

656
01:20:48,348 --> 01:20:50,183
One grows old.

657
01:20:51,976 --> 01:20:53,812
l knew a lot of fellas, friends of mine,

658
01:20:53,978 --> 01:20:55,814
they just wanted to live to open a bar.

659
01:20:55,939 --> 01:20:58,358
Had they lived,
would they have done it ?

660
01:21:01,569 --> 01:21:04,698
- Then they were spared their disillusion.
- Yeah, that's right.

661
01:21:06,783 --> 01:21:08,910
Who were these people ?
Friends of yours ?

662
01:21:11,788 --> 01:21:14,833
- l wouldn't hurt a friend.
- Was that my question ?

663
01:21:16,376 --> 01:21:17,669
That's right.

664
01:21:23,216 --> 01:21:26,553
Well, who are you ?

665
01:21:28,221 --> 01:21:31,683
A fella like you,
trying to make it to retirement.

666
01:21:31,850 --> 01:21:35,895
At the end of the day, we're likely
to be punished for our kindnesses.

667
01:21:36,021 --> 01:21:39,024
You don't have to worry about me.
l won't hurt you.

668
01:22:06,968 --> 01:22:09,220
The 47 ronin, do you know it ?

669
01:22:11,264 --> 01:22:16,728
47 samurai whose master
was betrayed and killed by another lord.

670
01:22:16,853 --> 01:22:20,357
They became ronin, masterless samurai,

671
01:22:20,523 --> 01:22:22,692
disgraced by another man's treachery.

672
01:22:24,194 --> 01:22:26,738
For three years they plotted,
pretending to be thieves,

673
01:22:26,905 --> 01:22:29,574
mercenaries, even madmen.

674
01:22:29,741 --> 01:22:32,077
That l didn't have time to do.

675
01:22:32,202 --> 01:22:34,579
And then one night they struck,
slipping into the castle

676
01:22:34,746 --> 01:22:36,664
of their lord's betrayer, killing him.

677
01:22:38,166 --> 01:22:40,585
Nice. l like that. My kind of job.

678
01:22:40,752 --> 01:22:42,671
There's something more.

679
01:22:44,297 --> 01:22:48,385
All 47 of them committed seppuku,

680
01:22:48,551 --> 01:22:51,846
ritual suicide,
in the courtyard of the castle.

681
01:22:52,013 --> 01:22:54,766
Well, that l don't like so much.

682
01:22:54,933 --> 01:22:58,019
- But you understand it ?
- What do you mean, l understand it ?

683
01:23:00,105 --> 01:23:04,734
The warrior code, the delight in the battle.
You understand that, yes ?

684
01:23:06,027 --> 01:23:08,905
But also something more.

685
01:23:09,030 --> 01:23:11,408
You understand there is something
outside yourself

686
01:23:11,533 --> 01:23:13,868
that has to be served.

687
01:23:14,035 --> 01:23:16,246
And when that need is gone,

688
01:23:16,413 --> 01:23:19,791
when belief has died, what are you ?

689
01:23:19,916 --> 01:23:21,876
A man without a master.

690
01:23:22,085 --> 01:23:24,879
Right now l'm a man
without a pay cheque.

691
01:23:25,046 --> 01:23:28,758
The ronin could have hired
themselves to new masters.

692
01:23:28,883 --> 01:23:31,011
They could have fought
for themselves.

693
01:23:31,177 --> 01:23:34,139
But they chose honour.
They chose myth.

694
01:23:35,348 --> 01:23:37,142
They chose wrong.

695
01:23:44,983 --> 01:23:47,485
Seppu... Seppu... what ?

696
01:23:47,652 --> 01:23:49,821
Yes, seppuku.

697
01:23:49,946 --> 01:23:52,157
Disembowelment.

698
01:23:52,323 --> 01:23:55,035
The sword goes in here.

699
01:24:05,170 --> 01:24:07,172
Are you sure this address is good ?

700
01:24:07,339 --> 01:24:09,215
Jean-Pierre gave it to me.

701
01:24:42,707 --> 01:24:46,169
Under the bridge by the river...

702
01:24:46,294 --> 01:24:48,963
How did you know
it was an ambush ?

703
01:24:49,089 --> 01:24:51,508
Whenever there is any doubt,
there is no doubt.

704
01:24:51,675 --> 01:24:53,510
That's the first thing they teach you.

705
01:24:57,305 --> 01:24:59,974
Who taught you ?

706
01:25:00,141 --> 01:25:03,269
l don't remember.
That's the second thing they teach you.

707
01:25:08,483 --> 01:25:10,735
All good things
come to those who wait.

708
01:25:41,558 --> 01:25:45,145
- Why is Gregor still alive ?
- He's taking them to the package.

709
01:26:09,753 --> 01:26:10,920
How ya doin' ?

710
01:26:18,803 --> 01:26:21,514
What are you...
What are you gonna do to me ?

711
01:26:21,681 --> 01:26:26,895
Let's just be calm for one more moment.
One more moment.

712
01:26:39,616 --> 01:26:41,659
Why ? Why ?

713
01:26:41,785 --> 01:26:43,828
You know why.

714
01:26:43,953 --> 01:26:46,081
No. You don't wanna do that.

715
01:26:49,918 --> 01:26:50,877
You can't.

716
01:26:55,840 --> 01:26:56,466
Get back !

717
01:26:58,093 --> 01:27:00,053
Get in the fucking car !

718
01:27:10,021 --> 01:27:11,564
Why didn't you shoot her ?

719
01:28:03,783 --> 01:28:05,493
Take the tunnel, now !

720
01:28:05,618 --> 01:28:07,579
Oh, Christ !

721
01:28:09,914 --> 01:28:12,000
Eh, merde !

722
01:31:20,522 --> 01:31:21,856
Come on ! Come on !

723
01:31:47,007 --> 01:31:48,925
All right, you fuck !

724
01:35:15,965 --> 01:35:18,301
Where could he be ?

725
01:35:18,426 --> 01:35:22,347
- Where could he be ?
- Hmm.

726
01:35:22,514 --> 01:35:25,934
The lrish and the Russians are looking
for him. So where does he go ?

727
01:35:26,059 --> 01:35:29,896
He goes to the Russians
to make the deal for the case.

728
01:35:30,021 --> 01:35:33,483
Gregor ain't comin' in unless
he can figure out a safe exchange.

729
01:35:33,650 --> 01:35:35,777
He knows they'll kill him for the case
rather than pay him for it.

730
01:35:35,902 --> 01:35:41,241
He's got to work it out soon
before the lrish find him.

731
01:35:42,617 --> 01:35:44,411
So where does he go ?

732
01:35:46,287 --> 01:35:48,123
You go to what you know.

733
01:35:51,710 --> 01:35:55,505
He's KGB.
He goes to one of his old safe houses.

734
01:35:57,007 --> 01:35:59,592
No, they're all blown.

735
01:35:59,759 --> 01:36:02,095
Where does he go ?

736
01:36:07,892 --> 01:36:11,271
So, you're on the run.
Where do you go ?

737
01:36:11,438 --> 01:36:13,314
Hmm ?

738
01:36:17,485 --> 01:36:21,865
Where's he been ? Where's he been ?
Where's he been ? Where's he been ?

739
01:36:33,668 --> 01:36:36,212
He made the fake case.

740
01:36:36,338 --> 01:36:38,673
He had the fake case made.

741
01:36:38,840 --> 01:36:42,260
Gregor. He had it made.

742
01:36:42,385 --> 01:36:44,929
He had to have had it made.

743
01:36:46,473 --> 01:36:49,559
ln Paris, before we went to Nice.

744
01:36:49,684 --> 01:36:51,478
He didn't have time to have it made.

745
01:36:51,603 --> 01:36:53,772
He bought something that looked like it,
then spray-painted it.

746
01:36:53,897 --> 01:36:56,441
Where did he get the spray ?
He never left the room.

747
01:36:56,566 --> 01:36:58,526
Where did he get the case ?

748
01:37:08,203 --> 01:37:10,413
Excusez-moi, monsieur.

749
01:37:31,768 --> 01:37:33,561
lt's a case for ice skates.

750
01:37:37,190 --> 01:37:39,067
Why ice skates ?

751
01:37:41,403 --> 01:37:43,363
And why would Gregor
know an ice-skate case ?

752
01:37:45,407 --> 01:37:47,867
He didn't have time to have it made.

753
01:37:48,034 --> 01:37:52,789
He didn't have time to have it made.
The Russians made it.

754
01:37:54,791 --> 01:37:57,335
The Russians made it.

755
01:38:00,505 --> 01:38:02,340
We're following the wrong people.

756
01:38:02,507 --> 01:38:05,385
We don't have to find Gregor.

757
01:38:05,552 --> 01:38:08,221
We find the Russians,
they will take us to him.

758
01:38:08,388 --> 01:38:12,225
You've lived in Paris
a long time. You know the people.

759
01:38:12,350 --> 01:38:15,353
- l get around.
- You meet the new Russians.

760
01:38:15,478 --> 01:38:19,357
You know how it is.
Ex-spies. Now it's Mafia.

761
01:38:20,275 --> 01:38:22,360
Under diplomatic cover.

762
01:38:23,945 --> 01:38:24,904
KGB ?

763
01:38:25,196 --> 01:38:26,156
Ex-KGB.

764
01:38:26,614 --> 01:38:31,161
Heavy hitters, gamblers,
lots ofmoney, big cars.

765
01:38:31,286 --> 01:38:32,662
They live like tsars.
Throw money away.

766
01:38:32,787 --> 01:38:34,622
Fur hats are expensive.

767
01:38:34,748 --> 01:38:40,128
- And bodyguards.
- Expensive coats, Dr Zhivago.

768
01:38:40,253 --> 01:38:43,381
l have a lot of work, no time.

769
01:38:44,924 --> 01:38:46,509
l understand.

770
01:38:48,303 --> 01:38:49,971
All right. Let's go.

771
01:38:50,930 --> 01:38:51,890
Okay.

772
01:38:59,105 --> 01:39:00,648
lt will be fine.

773
01:39:02,192 --> 01:39:04,027
The guy is gonna reach out.

774
01:39:04,152 --> 01:39:06,029
ls he any good ?

775
01:39:06,196 --> 01:39:09,032
Jean-Pierre says if it's Russian
and it's in Paris...

776
01:39:20,168 --> 01:39:23,546
lfl wanted to find Russians
in Paris this week,

777
01:39:23,672 --> 01:39:27,801
l'd go to the ice show.

778
01:40:41,875 --> 01:40:43,960
- Bonsoir, Pierre.
- Bonsoir.

779
01:40:44,085 --> 01:40:45,962
Je vais payer pour votre soeur.

780
01:40:46,087 --> 01:40:49,424
Oh, merci beaucoup,
Mademoiselle Kirilova.

781
01:40:55,972 --> 01:41:00,685
l'll trade you a cigarette for a favour.

782
01:41:01,269 --> 01:41:03,146
The favour is, steer clear ofthose guys.

783
01:41:03,271 --> 01:41:04,731
Who ? The Russians ?

784
01:41:11,279 --> 01:41:13,448
They sure throw their money around.

785
01:41:14,616 --> 01:41:15,658
Bonsoir.

786
01:41:15,784 --> 01:41:17,952
- Ça va ?
- Salut.

787
01:41:21,289 --> 01:41:23,124
- Bonsoir.
- Ah, bonsoir.

788
01:41:29,714 --> 01:41:34,010
The Russian is seeing Natacha Kirilova,
the star of the ice show.

789
01:41:34,135 --> 01:41:37,681
He spends every evening in the audience.

790
01:41:38,973 --> 01:41:40,433
How did you find that out ?

791
01:41:40,558 --> 01:41:43,812
We went to high school together.

792
01:42:18,096 --> 01:42:20,515
Mikhi, is everything all right ?

793
01:42:21,349 --> 01:42:22,726
Everything is fine.

794
01:42:23,977 --> 01:42:24,978
Sweet girl.

795
01:42:27,814 --> 01:42:28,773
Go. Go on.

796
01:42:47,792 --> 01:42:49,502
Ladies and gentlemen !

797
01:42:49,627 --> 01:42:52,881
We are veryproud to present...

798
01:42:53,006 --> 01:42:59,846
..two-time Olympic champion
and three-time World champion,...

799
01:42:59,971 --> 01:43:03,558
..Natacha Kirilova !

800
01:45:09,893 --> 01:45:11,770
Let's go.

801
01:45:25,158 --> 01:45:27,243
Wait out here.

802
01:45:32,248 --> 01:45:34,459
Yes, he is.

803
01:45:34,584 --> 01:45:36,628
Hello, Mikhi.

804
01:45:36,795 --> 01:45:40,757
- The meeting is not till later tonight.
- The meeting's now.

805
01:45:44,177 --> 01:45:45,720
You have the money ?

806
01:45:47,097 --> 01:45:50,975
Well, we were going to go back
to get it before the meet.

807
01:45:51,101 --> 01:45:52,185
l don't think so.

808
01:45:53,687 --> 01:45:55,563
You have the money ?

809
01:46:00,026 --> 01:46:02,987
l might have the money.
Where is the case ?

810
01:46:03,113 --> 01:46:07,450
No, you have to do it.
l couldn't live with myself.

811
01:46:20,463 --> 01:46:22,298
l have the money.

812
01:46:22,465 --> 01:46:24,926
We conclude this now
and part friends.

813
01:46:25,051 --> 01:46:26,803
Okay ?

814
01:46:29,723 --> 01:46:30,765
Where is the case ?

815
01:46:43,194 --> 01:46:45,030
l'd like to be paid now.

816
01:46:50,660 --> 01:46:52,787
No doubt.

817
01:46:57,584 --> 01:46:59,419
Now tell me the other part.

818
01:47:00,920 --> 01:47:03,048
The other part ?

819
01:47:03,214 --> 01:47:05,050
l'm leaving.

820
01:47:05,216 --> 01:47:08,053
l'm taking my fee and l'm leaving.

821
01:47:09,721 --> 01:47:12,766
l have a person with a rifle in the stadium.

822
01:47:13,016 --> 01:47:15,810
l've worked with her for years.
She never misses.

823
01:47:15,977 --> 01:47:18,897
l will call.

824
01:47:19,064 --> 01:47:21,358
l have to call within 45 seconds

825
01:47:21,524 --> 01:47:23,568
to say that l'm leaving,

826
01:47:23,735 --> 01:47:26,863
and then in another 10 minutes
to say that l'm safe.

827
01:47:28,573 --> 01:47:32,452
Should l be unable to call,
your friend will be shot.

828
01:47:42,337 --> 01:47:44,172
30 seconds, Mikhi.

829
01:47:45,632 --> 01:47:48,093
- We need to get inside.
- You can'tpass without badges.

830
01:47:55,475 --> 01:47:57,268
20 seconds.

831
01:48:07,987 --> 01:48:08,947
10 seconds.

832
01:48:38,226 --> 01:48:41,062
There were two ofthem.

833
01:48:41,187 --> 01:48:42,856
They were looking for those guys.

834
01:48:42,981 --> 01:48:45,108
Just a minute, sir !

835
01:49:01,708 --> 01:49:05,587
l am a Chilean citizen,
as you can see from mypassport.

836
01:49:05,712 --> 01:49:07,339
Merci.

837
01:49:45,835 --> 01:49:48,963
- Mama !
- Shh, shh, shh.

838
01:49:54,844 --> 01:49:56,429
Katchev !

839
01:49:56,554 --> 01:49:57,681
Qu'est-ce qui se passe ?

840
01:50:12,737 --> 01:50:13,697
Stay with him.

841
01:50:46,604 --> 01:50:49,107
Get out of here.
Get out of here !

842
01:50:49,274 --> 01:50:52,068
Get out of the car.
Walk away. Walk away !

843
01:50:52,193 --> 01:50:54,988
Walk away ! Go. Go.

844
01:50:55,113 --> 01:50:57,949
- l will if you will.
- Just go.

845
01:50:58,074 --> 01:51:00,493
Come with me.
Forget about the case.

846
01:51:04,956 --> 01:51:07,417
l didn't come for the case.
l came for your boss.

847
01:51:09,294 --> 01:51:11,838
l came for Seamus. l came for him.

848
01:51:13,256 --> 01:51:18,136
Just get out of here.
l never left. Don't you see ?

849
01:51:19,554 --> 01:51:21,848
Get out of the way !
Get out of the way !

850
01:51:30,231 --> 01:51:31,524
Get out of the way !

851
01:51:31,649 --> 01:51:32,942
This way is blocked.

852
01:52:00,804 --> 01:52:02,639
l can take you in or leave you here.

853
01:52:04,182 --> 01:52:05,392
There. That's him with the case.

854
01:52:05,517 --> 01:52:07,602
Sir ! Over here, please.

855
01:52:07,727 --> 01:52:08,436
Wait ! Wait !

856
01:52:16,111 --> 01:52:19,114
There are more back there !

857
01:52:56,443 --> 01:52:58,278
Stay where you are !
Stay where you are !

858
01:52:58,403 --> 01:53:02,240
Don't move ! Shut your fuckin' mouth up !
Shut your mouth !

859
01:53:16,296 --> 01:53:18,089
You stupid shite.

860
01:53:18,298 --> 01:53:21,801
You're a dead man.

861
01:53:44,366 --> 01:53:46,701
This is the BBC World Service.

862
01:53:46,868 --> 01:53:49,537
lt was announced today,
after almost 30 years

863
01:53:49,662 --> 01:53:52,999
ofbloody and seemingly intractable
civil conflict in Northern lreland,

864
01:53:53,124 --> 01:53:55,001
that a peace agreement
has been reached between

865
01:53:55,168 --> 01:53:58,338
the predominantly Protestant
government ofthat British-ruled enclave,

866
01:53:58,505 --> 01:54:01,007
and the lrish resistance...

867
01:54:05,845 --> 01:54:09,391
..have told CNN that it was
the apprehension and slaying

868
01:54:09,557 --> 01:54:14,354
in France ofthe lrish terrorist Seamus
O'Rourke, byparties still unknown,

869
01:54:14,479 --> 01:54:16,773
that contributed a stability,
largely allowing

870
01:54:16,898 --> 01:54:20,860
the negotiations to proceed
to their historic conclusion today.

871
01:54:21,027 --> 01:54:23,905
O'Rourke had earlier
been denounced by the lRA,

872
01:54:24,072 --> 01:54:28,118
the military wing ofSinn Fein,
as a rogue breakaway operative.

873
01:54:30,662 --> 01:54:33,957
Well, then, good knowin' ya.

874
01:54:44,718 --> 01:54:45,677
Hmm ?

875
01:54:45,802 --> 01:54:48,972
- l'm sorry ?
- You said something.

876
01:54:49,097 --> 01:54:52,559
l said she would not
be coming back here.

877
01:54:54,769 --> 01:54:59,190
Yeah. She would
not be coming back here, would she ?

878
01:55:05,488 --> 01:55:07,532
l can't even put my hand in my pocket
to pay the bill.

879
01:55:07,657 --> 01:55:09,784
l'll get it.

880
01:55:12,328 --> 01:55:14,122
l'll get the next one.

881
01:55:20,503 --> 01:55:22,213
What was in the case ?

882
01:55:22,464 --> 01:55:24,466
l don't remember.

883
01:55:25,842 --> 01:55:27,344
Lesson number two.

884
01:55:29,554 --> 01:55:31,389
Keep in touch.

885
01:55:49,949 --> 01:55:51,743
Let's go.

886
01:56:05,006 --> 01:56:07,759
No questions, no answers.

887
01:56:07,884 --> 01:56:09,969
That's the business we're in.

888
01:56:10,095 --> 01:56:12,347
You accept it and move on.

889
01:56:13,807 --> 01:56:16,559
Maybe that's lesson number three.
